1
00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:05,983
The SS team sent to catch the criminal
ended up getting caught themselves,

2
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:09,680
and only Ryotsu is left.
We've been utterly defeated.

3
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:15,705
Japan just isn't ready for a
special forces unit after all.

4
00:00:15,755 --> 00:00:17,034
It's extremely disappointing.

5
00:00:17,084 --> 00:00:20,880
Let's contact SGS9 back home
and ask for reinforcements.

6
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,440
The battle isn't over yet. I'm still here.

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:31,060
No way. Ukkari Hachibee alone
can't take down the enemy.

8
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,920
We really need someone like the
Windmill Mansion or Kagerou Oginn.

9
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:43,640
What?

10
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:52,900
The Windmill Mansion

11
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,060
That bulge down there isn't just for show.

12
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,820
When an incident breaks out on land,

13
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,700
a pair of swim trunks solves everything.

14
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,020
One of the Sanba Glass
special investigation unit.

15
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,920
Swim Trunks Detective!

16
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,140
I'm home.

17
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,320
Thirty.

18
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,120
There's a door, you know.

19
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,860
Don't go out of your way to punch
a hole in the wall to come in!

20
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,260
That voice...

21
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:18,220
So it's the flying monkey
from Tsuge this time?

22
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:36,400
I'm Umino Dodai,
captain of the Water Police Squad.

23
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,900
Dorubin,
whose trademark is his playful Yashioki cut.

24
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,480
These two

25
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,780
No, at this rate, those guys too...

26
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,320
Is this Kagerou Ogin?

27
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,200
No, it isn't.

28
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:05,360
What? The silhouette in
the window was a woman's.

29
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,400
And she's dressed decently, too.

30
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:10,400
Of everyone,
these guys are the biggest perverts.

31
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:13,500
Moonlight Power!

32
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,320
Don't tell me they're going to transform?

33
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,300
Just watch, it's hilarious.

34
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:33,960
This is

35
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,840
Make up!

36
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:40,760
Changing clothes...

37
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,460
A dazzling transformation
is a piece of cake.

38
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,460
Bathing my back in the energy of the moon,

39
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:48,500
with my wand of justice,
I cut through the darkness!

40
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,720
If it's a case in the sky, leave it to me.

41
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:53,080
Messenger from the moon,
in the name of moonlight,

42
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,860
You guys take too long.

43
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,660
Long time no see, Ryotsu.

44
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:04,200
Now that we of the Special Criminal Investigation Division,
Sanba Garasu, have arrived,

45
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,860
we'll arrest terrorists in no time.

46
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,520
Ryotsu, aren't they reliable guys?

47
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,840
Are these guys really reliable?

48
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:15,940
Westra's here!

49
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,660
Time to fuel up before the battle.

50
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,560
So that's what it is, after all.

51
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:29,000
Making Ukkari Hachibei trip like that,
he's quite the powerhouse.

52
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,040
Don't be impressed by it either.

53
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:36,180
You lot, support Ryotsu and
please rescue the hostages.

54
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,240
Japan's peace rests on your shoulders.

55
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:46,600
Yeah, well,
don't blame me if something happens to me.

56
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:52,360
The 100-story building is the bottleneck.

57
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:57,580
We'll burn all our energy
before we reach the top floor.

58
00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:02,140
If it were only ten floors,
I could arrest them all by myself.

59
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,980
Impossible.
Make the hundred floors into ten?

60
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:06,880
Turn a hundred floors into ten?

61
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,720
Well, it's not entirely impossible.

62
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:13,160
I have an idea.

63
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,600
Cheers!

64
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:22,520
In an hour we'll have ten trillion
yen and we'll be out of Japan for good.

65
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,740
That weird guy never showed up
to rescue them after all, did he?

66
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:31,820
He must have run off with his tail between his legs,
scared of us.

67
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:40,900
What's that?

68
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:55,780
Aaaah!

69
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:58,120
The shock of the Fuji TV telegram booth!

70
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:01,220
We're going to borrow that
spherical telegram booth for a bit.

71
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:04,160
Everyone inside, please move out promptly.

72
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,180
What?!

73
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:06,060
Alright.

74
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,160
Begin the wire-lock operation!

75
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,260
Understood.

76
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,080
Fire the wire!

77
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:20,780
Fire!

78
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,580
Fire!

79
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,320
Okay, good, pull it out!

80
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,720
Roger.

81
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,280
Come on, hurry up and get here!

82
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:56,060
Aoshima, Kisser, Squee,
whatever you do, don't fall over!

83
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,000
We have to protect them with our lives.

84
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,820
Alright, good, keep it up!

85
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,480
You terrorists, just you wait and see!

86
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,240
W-what is that?

87
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:18,020
C-Colonel Kepel!

88
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:20,560
What on earth is Yotsu planning to do?

89
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:28,540
Right! Attach the helicopter to the side!

90
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:41,400
Fire the special suction wire!

91
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,200
Yes!

92
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,340
Alright! Here we go! It's a Daruma Otoshi!

93
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,860
Alright, one more!

94
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,160
Do it!

95
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:23,940
Good, nice work, everyone!

96
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,520
Keep it up and keep lowering that building!

97
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:27,680
Roger.

98
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,740
What have they done?

99
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:46,160
Damn it, what are they doing?!

100
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:50,000
The building's getting shorter!

101
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,100
What?!

102
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,260
Only someone who'd pull
a stunt this reckless

103
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:56,500
is Ryo-san!

104
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:06,160
Good, if it's this low,
we can storm in easily!

105
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:08,480
Hang on, you terrorist scum!

106
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:18,680
We're storming in, so Big Dolphin
and Big Gekkou, get into position.

107
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:28,500
Right, let's go! Open-crotch... Hey, what is this?!
If you want to team up with me, you've got to wear these.

108
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:36,280
That again?! If you won't talk, forget this whole deal.
Fine, I'll talk, okay?!

109
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:39,900
Is it really alright to let
these guys do it like this?

110
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:43,080
Under the circumstances,
let's leave it to them.

111
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,220
Let's go!

112
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:50,120
That SS guy is storming in with another one!

113
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,160
And he's naked!

114
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,000
What?

115
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,380
Thunder Gosher strikes back!

116
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:56,020
Got it.

117
00:08:58,140 --> 00:09:00,800
Just as I thought, Lord Ryo came to save us!

118
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:04,640
But why is there another man naked with him?

119
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,020
Could it be... could it be?

120
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:11,940
Don't say it.
I don't even want to hear that name.

121
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:16,600
How about this?
This outfit's lighter, isn't it?

122
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,140
Shut up and hurry up and run!

123
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:26,140
Look! The 95th floor's staircase is
perfectly sitting on top of the 5th floor!

124
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:27,380
Magnificent.

125
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,820
Alright, let's go!

126
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,000
That's enough.

127
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:40,600
Trying to take on rifles
with bare hands and dancing?

128
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,420
What a bunch of idiots.

129
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:46,920
What do you think you're doing?

130
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,100
No need for projectile weapons.

131
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,820
Don't panic.

132
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,180
Hey, hey.

133
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:04,780
Excuse me, it's time for my nutrition break.

134
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,680
Stop with that banana!

135
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:10,440
Munch, munch, gulp.

136
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,540
I hate fighting.

137
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:16,000
Let's get naked and talk this over.

138
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,280
What?

139
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:22,220
Come on, you too,
let's get naked and talk it out.

140
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,340
Is this guy out of his mind or what?

141
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,380
There's nothing to be embarrassed about.

142
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:31,920
When people are born,
they're all stark naked.

143
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:36,020
Let's talk with the pure heart of a baby.

144
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:38,480
Don't come near us!

145
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:42,920
Ryotsu, you too, take off your underwear.

146
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,580
No way!

147
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,380
If you take yours off,
they'll take theirs off too.

148
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,720
I don't get the logic at all.

149
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:52,900
To get the other side naked,
we must first get naked ourselves.

150
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,060
That's just your own logic, you know.

151
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:56,260
Just take it off already!

152
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,180
Fine, fine, I'll take it off, all right?

153
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,840
Geez, what an outrageous helper we've got!

154
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:08,900
Hey, what the hell are you doing!

155
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:12,520
You're already an intermediate.
There's no need to hide it.

156
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,880
Don't go raising my rank without permission!

157
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:16,660
Damn it, if it's come to this,
I'm going all in!

158
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:18,040
How about that!

159
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:21,700
There, you're not
embarrassed anymore, right?

160
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:26,720
Don't come near me!

161
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,340
We don't have that kind of hobby!

162
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,680
Don't be so shy.

163
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:35,440
Let it dangle and you'll be freed in body and mind,
it feels great!

164
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:37,860
Akishoko

165
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,560
Now!

166
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:42,380
Victory!

167
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:42,820
Victory!

168
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:57,940
That was surprisingly easy.

169
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:01,200
As always, a terrifying technique.

170
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:04,980
Trey!

171
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:06,920
Senpai!

172
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:10,360
Ryo-sama! You really did come after all.

173
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:12,380
What happened to the terrorists?

174
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:13,940
They're planning to escape.

175
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,720
They're taking their father to the rooftop!

176
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:18,900
Abdalla, the brother of Adayada,
is coming to pick them up by helicopter.

177
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:21,800
Abdalla was in Japan?

178
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:24,240
Kaipan Deka, leave this to us!

179
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,700
Ryo-sama, be careful!

180
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,580
Dolphin Digger, second operation, start!

181
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,020
Understood.

182
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,460
Hey, hurry up and walk!

183
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,440
You've caused us a lot of trouble.

184
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,940
Sorry, bro.

185
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,460
Just hurry up and get in!

186
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:56,560
Mr. Ryotsu!

187
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:59,060
I won't let you escape! Dolphin Dagger!

188
00:12:59,620 --> 00:12:59,920
What?

189
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:06,880
The southern sea no one knows

190
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:09,960
Joe, this is no time to be singing
"Michiru"! Hurry up!

191
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:12,400
You're impatient, aren't you?

192
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,240
Welcome!

193
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,720
My companion is Ryuichiro.

194
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,800
No, I mean, Ryuichiro is me.

195
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:28,080
My companion is Ryuichiro.

196
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:28,700
Shut up!

197
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:31,420
I'm not some ugly guy.

198
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:33,240
I'm not that kind of man either.

199
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,160
Which one's the real one? I have no clue.

200
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,300
Melan, please, get in the room.

201
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,280
Hurry up! I'll make you come!

202
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:48,060
Damn, I never thought they'd take everyone!

203
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,720
Moonlight Detective, come quick!

204
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,920
Roger.

205
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,640
Alright, chase the helicopter!

206
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:01,840
Idiot, why are you coming down?

207
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:05,360
What are you doing?
Hurry up and chase the helicopter!

208
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:10,440
Come on, change into this.

209
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,440
Not again.

210
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:15,640
If I go out in such a vulgar outfit,
I'll be laughed at.

211
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:18,660
I'll transform too, so hurry up and change.

212
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:20,360
Never mind that, just hurry up!

213
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,940
Moonlight Power!

214
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:35,140
Hurry up already.

215
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:42,660
What's with that outfit?

216
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,500
Allow me to explain.

217
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:50,540
When Moonlight Detective wears the bunny girl costume,
his hearing gets boosted tenfold!

218
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:52,160
I can hear them! I can hear them!

219
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:53,420
Their helicopter is

220
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,700
in that direction.

221
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:57,940
Sure enough.

222
00:14:57,940 --> 00:14:59,220
You can see it, can't you?

223
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:01,680
Don't bother transforming,
just hurry and chase them!

224
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:04,380
Then, into the pursuit costume

225
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:11,760
Leave it to you guys. I'll pilot.

226
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:19,680
They're chasing us! Speed up more!

227
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,600
We're at the limit, we can't go any faster.

228
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:26,680
I'll take over the controls.
You go take care of those guys.

229
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:28,900
Got it. Move aside for a sec.

230
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,960
Right, we're shooting them down!

231
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:42,720
Damn it!

232
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:45,200
His skills are better than
Nakagawa's and Reiko's.

233
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:52,660
We did it!

234
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,660
Aim for the engine next.

235
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:55,380
OK.

236
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:58,700
No way.

237
00:15:59,180 --> 00:15:59,740
What's wrong?

238
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:02,240
We shot through the fuselage,
but it's still alive!

239
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,620
That can't be possible.

240
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,500
Take better aim and try again!

241
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,700
It's a monster!

242
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,360
We're out of ammo!

243
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,860
So we've finally run out of ammo!

244
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,060
They were all my figures after all!

245
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:35,720
No way, it's for real!

246
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:38,580
Here we go! Now it's our turn!

247
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,380
Go, bazooka!

248
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:51,680
I'm going!

249
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,020
Allow me to explain!

250
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,900
When Moonlight Detective
transforms into this costume,

251
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,980
she can pilot with
incredibly acrobatic skill.

252
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:11,680
Here we go!

253
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,560
How about that?
That's the skill of Full Thirty!

254
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:27,680
Got it! I get it, so please stop already!

255
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,780
Ugh, how disgusting!

256
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:35,980
Don't leave me behind yet!

257
00:17:35,980 --> 00:17:36,420
There we go!

258
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,700
I need to shake out my shoulders.

259
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,820
I feel sick.

260
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:56,140
They're flying too well, I can't hit them!

261
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:58,200
Alright, time to fight back!

262
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,360
I can't control the aircraft!

263
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,260
What?!

264
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:09,740
Damn it!

265
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:10,640
Bail out!

266
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,020
Yes.

267
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,940
What's going to happen to this?

268
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:27,300
Moonlight Detective!

269
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,260
We have to rescue Nakagawa's
old man and the lookalikes!

270
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:31,740
Roger.

271
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:35,400
We're saving you now, you hear?

272
00:18:37,140 --> 00:18:39,125
Alright,

273
00:18:39,175 --> 00:18:45,280
Tojichi's been rescued!

274
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:47,960
Those bastards, don't let them get away!

275
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,320
What?

276
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,840
Hey you lot, everyone jump off the ship!

277
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:10,960
If it comes to this, Scare!

278
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:16,240
Why would you just escape over there?

279
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,160
Y-yes!

280
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:18,440
What's that?

281
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,980
Nobody knows.

282
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,160
It's that guy again!

283
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:26,600
Shit!

284
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:28,880
The South Seas

285
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:30,300
You can't escape anymore!

286
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:31,600
Shut up!

287
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:40,780
Dolphin Dagger counterattack!

288
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:41,580
Okay!

289
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,760
Hey, Dolphin! Come on!

290
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:48,860
Only I'm pink!

291
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,560
Naru naru!

292
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:56,055
Today,

293
00:19:56,105 --> 00:20:00,060
Pinka-chan, the pink dolphin,
has also come to cheer us on.

294
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:02,120
You know her?
The one from the late-night show!

295
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:09,920
Look!

296
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:13,580
You idiot!
What are you doing, pleasing the enemy?

297
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:17,540
It's just a standard gag.
Next time, we'll do it for real.

298
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:22,760
Here it goes!

299
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,340
What do you think you're doing?!

300
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:30,980
Let's go!

301
00:20:48,540 --> 00:20:51,700
Isn't there a weapon more
powerful than the Dolphin Dagger?

302
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,360
There is one,
but I won't take responsibility for it.

303
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,320
Tomahawk!

304
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:57,960
Tomahawk!

305
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,080
Tomahawk!

306
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,220
Tomahawk!

307
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:04,640
Tomahawk!

308
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:04,680
Tomahawk!

309
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,040
Tomahawk!

310
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:06,100
Tomahawk!

311
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,760
Aaaaaah!

312
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,220
Everyone is under arrest.

313
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:47,920
We surrender.

314
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:56,720
Colonel Kepel, the operation is over.

315
00:21:57,660 --> 00:22:02,040
Mr. Ryotsu, thank you. Thank you so much.

316
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:07,040
We broke the building, but compared to ten trillion yen,
that's no problem, right?

317
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:10,280
I don't mind, but this gentleman here...

318
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:13,540
We've come as representatives.

319
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:15,480
T-Tsuyuki-san...

320
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:19,320
Our company's worth will have to decrease.

321
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,760
200 billion yen?

322
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:24,800
Hey, you've got to be kidding!

323
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,900
There's no way we have that kind of money!

324
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:29,260
Oh right, what about Nakagawa's father?

325
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,660
Farewell.

326
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:32,800
Let's meet again in ten years.

327
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,760
Goodbye, Dad.

328
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:37,360
Hey, don't send them off without permission!

329
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:38,940
Colonel Kepel.

330
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,420
Please do something about this!

331
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:43,400
I don't know anything about it.

332
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,880
Don't say that! Hey! Swim-trunks Detective!

333
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:49,080
What? An incident?

334
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,580
Alright, I'm going right now.

335
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:53,320
See you later.

336
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:56,340
Hey! No phone call came through at all!

337
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:57,580
Don't run away!

338
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:00,120
Damn it! Moonlight Detective!

339
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,440
Lake One!

340
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:04,620
Flo-Ense Joyner!

341
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:08,560
Anyway, your gags are way too old!

342
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:09,940
Allow me to explain.

343
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:13,800
Moonlight Detective gets faster on
his feet when he wears this costume.

344
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:16,020
Hey, it's filthy!

345
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,920
Dolphin Detective!

346
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:21,240
Nobody knows that.

347
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:23,440
"Nobody knows" is not a valid answer,
you know.

348
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:24,940
Come on.

349
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:29,720
Let's make you pay up.

350
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:36,600
Special Security Team, my foot!

351
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,840
Something like Dwai Kiraider!

352
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:09,060
Thrilling, a flash of inspiration

353
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:12,020
bouncing with joy, all gathered together

354
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:14,960
action and flying away

355
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:19,840
the most amazing power of all

356
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:22,280
Everyone, gather!

357
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:25,600
if you come here

358
00:24:26,520 --> 00:24:28,720
like a dream

359
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:31,920
the final energy

360
00:24:33,140 --> 00:24:35,880
gazing at tomorrow, the star of hope

361
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:39,320
painting the universe,
if you stand on the ground

362
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:43,020
the star of Kameari is coming,
and that's strange

363
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:46,740
Is this good enough?

364
00:24:46,740 --> 00:24:48,240
Like hell it is!

